Wrong transaction usage leads to deadlocks, negative inventory, and duplicate orders. Claude Code generates safe transaction design automatically from your CLAUDE.md. # Database Transaction Rules - Multi-table writes always wrapped in a transaction - No I/O (HTTP calls, file reads) inside transactions - Keep transactions as short as possible - Low contention → optimistic locking (version number column) - High contention → SELECT FOR UPDATE (pessimistic) - Always acquire locks in the same table order - SET statement_timeout = '5s' on all transactions - External services (Stripe, email) → Saga pattern with compensation
